<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One text block on a single printed page. At the top, a centred title in several lines under an ornamental border. Below it, one verse passage, left-aligned, opening with a decorated initial. The signature mark stands at the right after the last line. Page number at the top right. No running head.</layout>
  <page_number>177</page_number>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>M. j.[?]</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">MARTINO MARLOREO, BARRENSI CAVSIDICO,</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2">impuro Apostatae, Euangeli-</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="2">cae veritatis persecutori</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="2">acerrimo,</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="2">EPITAPHIVM I. I. B. posuit.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>T[?]ANDEM Causidicum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>tacere Parca Iussit Marloreum bonis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>benigna, Quos Barri prius impotente</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>lingua, Et gannitibus impiis, profanis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Impurus canis allatravit usque.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Quos furens odio Vatiniano,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Fictis criminibus, calumniisque,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Longis vociferationibusque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Vexavit Sycophanta turbulentus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Inquietior Adria inquieto,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Infanis violentior procellis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Thracio Diomede, vel Cyclope</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Humani sitientior cruoris,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Poenis perfidior dolosiorque,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Et Thrasone superbior Terenti[?],</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Iracundior invido Catello,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Interdum quoque blandior Catella,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Vel risu meretricis exoleta.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The title line "impuro" is struck through by a horizontal line in the print; it is kept here as printed. The decorated initial is taken to be T, but this is uncertain. "Terenti" is printed "Terentl" and may be a misprint. "impijs" is printed with j after i and is spelled as the vowel i here. The signature mark at the right is read as "M. j." and is uncertain.</notes>
</page>
